---
title: "Reusing an actor id after state loss: two writes share one name"
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant L0 as A
    participant L1 as B
    Note over L0: write<br/>A:1→"x"
    L0->>L1: #8203;
    Note over L1: sync<br/>A:1→"x"
    Note over L0: state lost<br/>∅
    Note over L0: write<br/>A:1→"y"
    Note over L0: both writes are dot A:1: the reborn replica reissued a name it had already used
    L0->>L1: #8203;
    Note over L1: sync<br/>A:1→"x"
    L1->>L0: #8203;
    Note over L0: sync<br/>A:1→"y"
    Note over L1,L0: B keeps "x" and A keeps "y": each believes it already holds the other's write, so they never converge
